 "qualification_statement": "Historical CLI/scheduled releases (C1) keep their bounded qualification: a small fixed-geometry fixture (4x6 dense cells, two fixed layers) ran the full public example to completion on NumPy, Numba and CUDA and resumed exactly. Separately, the Native Phase 2 Python API (evolving floating soil profile on the actual MAPLE bed, persistent W/J/I across native events and daily updates, optional every-N-day moisture output, closed-parent physical files; NumPy/Numba/CUDA, Dense and native Windowed) is independently qualified at a bounded scope on its clean source package (111 CPU/host and 39 actual-GPU controls, 18 portable source guards, a seven-day N=3 example saving days 3 and 6). It is a native API, not a command or YAML key of the historical CLI, and not a full scheduled MAPLE-SYRUP-LEAF simulation. No field validation, large-domain memory fit, general repeated-storm recovery, integrated wind clock is claimed for the Phase 2 API (that edition's statement; vegetation-cover feedback is treated separately below). Phase 2.5 (accepted at a bounded scope by Root's separate receipt): the native Python vegetation feedback (LEAF species receiving-weight trait, canopy/root projection, explicit site-control binding, compact cached recipe, zero-time vegetation generation on a completed boundary, water-free held context, vegetation-attributed every-N diagnostic frames) and the closed-parent physical checkpoint of a vegetated head, verified with 714 CPU and 37 actual-GPU tests on the exact 180-file source. It is a native Python API, not a command, YAML key or scheduler schema. No field validation, catchment-scale fit, scheduled three-model run, general repeated-storm recovery, vegetation-aware wind carry, GPU or Windowed wind is claimed.",
